  "challenge": {
    "title": "Bargaining and Getting There",
    "instructions": "Write and say a short Egyptian conversation of at least 10 lines. It must ask a price, bargain at least once, agree on a price, hail a taxi or ask about a bus, say where you want to go, and ask about the fare or the time. Use at least 8 target phrases from this unit and include both a masculine-address form and a feminine-address form.",
    "required_elements": [
      "A price question using بكام ده؟ or بكام الكيلو؟",
      "At least one attempt to lower the price, using نزّل شوية or فيه خصم؟",
      "An agreement using ماشي or آخر سعر.",
      "Hailing transport using فاضي؟ or naming تاكسي or أتوبيس.",
      "A destination using عايز أروح or وديني على.",
      "A question about fare or time using الأجرة كام؟ or الطريق هياخد قد إيه؟",
